Open a file
vi filename

If file does not exist → it will be created.

Modes in VI editor

VI editor has 3 modes:

Mode	Purpose
Normal mode	navigation & commands (default)
Insert mode	typing/editing text
Command mode	save, quit operations

Enter insert mode:

i

Exit insert mode:

Esc
Insert / Write text

Press:

i

Start typing.

Save and Quit
Command	Meaning
:w	save file
:q	quit
:wq	save and quit
:q!	quit without saving

(Press Esc before typing :)

Delete operations
Command	Action
x	delete single character
dd	delete entire line
D	delete from cursor to end of line
Copy & Paste
Command	Action
yy	copy (yank) current line
p	paste below cursor
P	paste above cursor
Navigation (Scrolling)
Command	Action
Ctrl + u	scroll up
Ctrl + d	scroll down
gg	go to first line
G	go to last line
Move Cursor
Key	Move
h	left
l	right
k	up
j	down
Search inside file
/word

Press n → next match
Press N → previous match

Undo / Redo
Command	Action
u	undo
Ctrl + r	redo
Important Tip

Always remember:

Press Esc before giving any : command (save/quit), otherwise it will not work.
